{"type":"text","timestamp":1788226151775,"sessionID":"ses_fa570d749ffeZ0JayvJr5mQkae","part":{"id":"prt_05a958b22001iKATFknxUzGfRc","messageID":"msg_05a9582b5001tildflbJRMIvfp","sessionID":"ses_fa570d749ffeZ0JayvJr5mQkae","type":"text","text":"Done. The Books REST API is implemented per TASK.md using only the Python standard library (per `stack.json`):\n\n- **`app.py`** — `ThreadingHTTPServer` + `sqlite3` store with all endpoints: `POST/GET /books` (with `?author=` case-insensitive filter), `GET/PUT/DELETE /books/{id}`, and `GET /health`. Full validation (title/author required non-empty, year must be integer, isbn must be string), correct status codes (201 + `Location`, 204, 400/404/405), configurable via `PORT`/`BOOKS_DB` env vars.\n- **`test_app.py`** — 22 integration tests booting a real server on an ephemeral port with a temp DB; all pass (`python3 -m pytest -v` → 22 passed).\n- **`README.md`** — setup, run instructions, endpoint table, validation rules, and curl examples.\n- **`requirements.txt`** — empty (stdlib only).\n\nA live curl smoke test confirmed create (201), filter, update (200), delete (204), 404s, and 400 validation errors behave correctly.","time":{"start":1788226145058,"end":1788226151770}}}
